+# Generate module 17 lesson 17 ceiling break scene asset
+
+## Goal
+
+Generate one course scene PNG at `course-assets/scenes/module-17/m17_L17_b06_ceiling-break.png`.
+
+## Scope
+
+- Use the attached BMH course doodle references and locked flat sticker-sheet style.
+- Use gpt-image-2 through the built-in image generation workflow.
+- Create one 1600 x 900 PNG.
+- Show a simple doodle bar chart with exactly three vertical bars rising left to right.
+- Make the bars cream, yellow, then tall orange.
+- Include one horizontal dashed black ceiling line.
+- Make the tall orange bar punch through the ceiling line with a few clean line fragments at the break point.
+- Leave clean cornflower-blue space on the left for code-rendered overlays.
+- Use thick wobbly black outlines, rounded simple shapes, flat fills only, and the locked palette: cornflower blue, yellow, orange, cream, white, and black.
+- Avoid people, faces, text, words, letters, numbers, symbols, labels, ambient doodles, motion marks, icons, random props, gradients, texture, shadows, lighting, and perspective depth.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Confirm the file exists at the requested path.
+- Confirm the file is a PNG at 1600 x 900.
+- Confirm local palette flattening leaves only locked course colors.
+- Visually inspect for the three-bar chart, broken dashed ceiling, clean left blue space, no people, no text, no symbols, and no decorative clutter.
